==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sexy Bathtub Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Luxury Bath Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bath Cat is functionally a mix between [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]. It deals triple of Elemental Duelist's damage and comes with a hefty cost of long cooldown and foreswing. Use this cat as support alongside your King Dragons, or as an offensive ranger unit for your stacks of Elemental Duelists on Red-heavy stages.

Like King Dragon, it is also possible to stack Bath Cats up with protection from meatshields, creating very high DPS output against Reds. Although, this will be more difficult due to the longer cooldown.

==='''True Form'''===
Luxury Bath Cat gains improved health and a faster attack rate. Surprisingly, the improved health is by almost 10,000, reaching 20,400 at level 30, above-average compared to most other Super Rare Cats. The improved attack rate is not as good of an improvement, as Luxury Bath Cat still attacks quite slowly and their attack animation stays the same. The most the improved attack rate gives Luxury Bath Cat is an increase in DPS of about 500 at level 30, 35% more than their second form.

==='''Talents'''===
Resist Waves, Resist Weaken and Health Up will rarely come into play in a relevant way, so you can avoid getting them. The [[Knockback|knockback]] talent changes this unit's role, making it better at fending off against Red enemies, but removing the possibility to attain great DPS from stacking or to synergize with the likes of [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]. This leaves Damage Up as the only good talent to have, as it is a general improvement to its performance.

